# Task Manager API - basic test file (REST Client extension for VS Code)
#
# How to use:
#   1. Start the database (docker compose up -d) and the server (npm run start:dev).
#   2. Send the requests from top to bottom, one at a time ("Send Request").
#   3. Every title says which status code to expect.
#   4. Ids and tokens are copied automatically from earlier responses.
#   5. Tokens expire after 1 hour. If you get 401, send section A again.
#
# Actors:
#   owner  = test@example.com    creates the project
#   member = maria@example.com   gets invited to the project
#
# Only fake data lives in this file. Never paste real tokens or passwords here.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000


################################################################
# A. SETUP: users and logins
################################################################

### A1. Register the owner (201 the first time, 409 if it already exists - both are fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "name": "Owner",
  "password": "fake-password"
}

### A2. Register the member (201 the first time, 409 afterwards - both are fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "maria@example.com",
  "name": "Maria",
  "password": "fake-password-123"
}

### A3. Register with invalid data (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "abc",
  "name": "",
  "password": "123"
}

### A4. Login as owner (200, returns accessToken)
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "fake-password"
}

### A5. Login as member (200, returns accessToken)
# @name memberLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "maria@example.com",
  "password": "fake-password-123"
}

### A6. Login with a wrong password (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### A7. Who am I? Owner (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### A8. Protected endpoint without a token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

################################################################
# B. PROJECTS: the owner does CRUD
################################################################

### B1. Create a project (201, the owner also becomes a member with role OWNER)
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Website",
  "description": "Test project"
}

### B2. Create a project with an empty name (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": ""
}

### B3. Create a project without a token (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Website"
}

### B4. List my projects (200, contains the new project)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### B5. Get one project (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### B6. Get a project that does not exist (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### B7. Get a project with an id that is not a number (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### B8. Update only the name (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Website v2"
}

### B9. Update with an empty name (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": ""
}

### B10. Try to change the owner through the body (200, the ownerId field is ignored)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Website v3",
  "ownerId": 99
}

### B11. Someone who is NOT a member asks for the project (404, it does not exist for her)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### B12. The same person lists her projects (200, empty list [])
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

################################################################
# C. MEMBERS: invitations and roles
################################################################

### C1. Owner invites Maria (201, role MEMBER, no password in the answer)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}/members
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "email": "maria@example.com"
}

### C2. Invite the same person again (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}/members
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "email": "maria@example.com"
}

### C3. Invite an email that has no account (404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}/members
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com"
}

### C4. Owner lists the members (200, two entries: OWNER and MEMBER)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### C5. Now Maria can see the project (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### C6. Maria (member) tries to rename the project (403: she is known, but not allowed)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Renamed by member"
}

### C7. Maria (member) tries to invite someone (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}/members
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

################################################################
# D. TASKS: owner and member work on the same project
################################################################

### D1. Owner creates a task (201, status is TODO)
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Design homepage",
  "description": "First draft",
  "projectId": {{createProject.response.body.id}}
}

### D2. Create a task with projectId as text (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Bad task",
  "projectId": "abc"
}

### D3. Create a task in a project that does not exist (404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Ghost task",
  "projectId": 999999
}

### D4. Maria (member) creates a task too (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Write copy",
  "projectId": {{createProject.response.body.id}}
}

### D5. List the tasks of the project (200, two tasks)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?projectId={{createProject.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### D6. List tasks without projectId (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### D7. Get one task (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### D8. Change the status to DONE (200, updatedAt changes)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "status": "DONE"
}

### D9. Change the status to a value that is not allowed (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "status": "FINISHED"
}

### D10. Try to move the task to another project (200, the projectId field is ignored)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Design homepage v2",
  "projectId": 999999
}

################################################################
# E. DELETING: a task, then the whole project (cascade)
################################################################

### E1. Maria (member) tries to delete the project (403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### E2. Owner deletes a task (204, no body)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### E3. The deleted task is gone (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### E4. Owner deletes the project (204, its remaining tasks and members are deleted too)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### E5. The deleted project is gone (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{createProject.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
